# =============================================================================
# CODEOWNERS - Folder-based ownership rules
#
# This is a TEMPLATE. No owners are assigned by default, so a fresh repository
# never ships with invalid CODEOWNERS entries (a rule with no valid owner is a
# GitHub error and cannot satisfy "Require review from Code Owners").
#
# To enable code-owner review:
#   1. Uncomment the rule(s) you want below.
#   2. Replace @your-org/your-team with a real @user or @org/team that has
#      write access to this repository.
#   3. (Optional) Enable: Settings → Branches → Branch protection →
#      "Require review from Code Owners".
#
# PRECEDENCE: the LAST matching rule wins. Put broad defaults first, then more
# specific overrides below.
# =============================================================================


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 0) GLOBAL DEFAULT - fallback owner for any unmatched file.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# *                                    @your-org/your-team


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1) REPOSITORY GOVERNANCE & AUTOMATION
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# /.github/                            @your-org/your-team
# /.github/workflows/                  @your-org/your-team
# /assets/                             @your-org/your-team
# /.devcontainer/                      @your-org/your-team


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2) APPLICATION SOURCE & TESTS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# /src/                                @your-org/your-team
# /tests/                              @your-org/your-team


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3) DOCUMENTATION
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# /docs/                               @your-org/your-team
